ers.","zh":null},{"en":"The member companies of AEP have contractual, financial and other business relationships with the other member companies, such as participation in AEP savings and retirement plans and tax returns, sales of electricity and transportation and handling of fuel. The member companies of AEP also obtain certain accounting, administrative, information systems, engineering, financial, legal, maintenance and other services at cost from a common provider, AEPSC.","zh":null}],"markets":[{"en":"AEP's primary business is the generation, transmission and distribution of electricity. Within its Vertically Integrated Utilities segment, AEP centrally dispatches generation assets and manages its overall utility operations on an integrated basis because of the substantial impact of cost-based rates and regulatory oversight applicable to each public utility subsidiary. Intersegment sales and transfers are generally based on underlying contractual arrangements and agreements. AEP's reportable segments are as follows:","zh":null},{"en":"The remainder of AEP's activities are presented as Corporate and Other, which is not considered a reportable segment. See Note 9 - Business Segments for additional information on AEP's segments.","zh":null}],"customers":[{"en":"fossil fuel costs for the Vertically Integrated Utilities increased 0.5% on a dollar per MMBtu basis from 2024. AEP's resource mix is driven by the needs and desires of the states AEP serves and continued focus on cost effective economic dispatch to AEP's customers.","zh":null}],"competition":[{"en":"The Vertically Integrated Utilities primarily generate, transmit and distribute electricity to their retail customers in their service territories. These sales are made at rates approved by the state utility commissions of the states in which they operate, and in some instances, approved by the FERC, and are not subject to competition from other vertically integrated public utilities. Other than AEGCo, the Vertically Integrated Utilities hold franchises or other rights that effectively grant the exclusive ability to provide electric service in various municipalities and regions in their service areas.","zh":null},{"en":"The Vertically Integrated Utilities compete with self-generation and with distributors of other energy sources, such as natural gas, fuel oil, renewables and coal, within their service areas. The primary factors in such competition are price, reliability of service and the capability of customers to utilize alternative sources of energy other than electric power. With respect to competing generators and self-generation, the public utility subsidiaries of AEP believe that they currently maintain a competitive position.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Vertically Integrated Utilities","val":12819000000,"zh":"Vertically Integrated Utilities"},{"name":"Transmission & Distribution Companies","val":6147000000,"zh":"Transmission & Distribution Companies"},{"name":"Generation & Marketing","val":2762000000,"zh":"Generation & Marketing"},{"name":"Transmission Operations","val":2377000000,"zh":"Transmission Operations"},{"name":"AEP Transmission Holdco","val":2377000000,"zh":"AEP Transmission Holdco"}],"total":21876000000},"prod":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Retail","val":16000000000,"zh":"Retail"},{"name":"Electricity","val":12556000000,"zh":"Electricity"},{"name":"Residential","val":7754000000,"zh":"Residential"},{"name":"Transmissionand Distribution Utilities Revenues","val":6097000000,"zh":"Transmissionand Distribution Utilities Revenues"},{"name":"Wholesaleand Competitive","val":5220000000,"zh":"Wholesaleand Competitive"},{"name":"Commercial","val":4694000000,"zh":"Commercial"},{"name":"Industrial","val":3250000000,"zh":"Industrial"},{"name":"Generation & Marketing Revenues","val":2697000000,"zh":"Generation & Marketing Revenues"},{"name":"Marketing Competitive Retailand Renewable","val":2397000000,"zh":"Marketing Competitive Retailand Renewable"},{"name":"Wholesale Transmission","val":1603000000,"zh":"Wholesale Transmission"}],"total":21876000000}},"peers":["SO","D","DUK","EXC","ED"]}}